<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7533"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 16, 2005 - 6:23 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I have been reading threads on the seperate victims. I believe we need to link them together. It is possible that Nancy and Vickie knew each other, could have went to church together. The Ghostbuster team only mapped the actual area of the victims that they knew were BTK, What happened to the other unsolved murders? BTK&#39;s number is 3 If we try to add some of the other victims into the equation that were strangled, or stabbed three times, we can get a better Idea of the location were he lived. You have to rule out, the fire starter and any other crime that doesn&#39;t follow the MO. So I am going to go to the unsolved cases at the beginning of this site and see if we can get a more detailed idea of where BTK lived. I ask Christa to see if anymore of the Victims went to her church, and I ask Bookworm to work on the mapping. If the rest of you could help me with the other victims, I think we will see a link. We know he killed more people.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
