<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7650"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 17, 2005 - 12:24 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Embersage, I don&#39;t think there is anything that links all the victims to one common denominator except that they lived in Wichita. By that I mean I don&#39;t think that BTK was for example someone like a gas station attendent and all the victims at one time or another came to his gas station. <BR> I think they began as random but I do believe there is a possiblity that two of them may be linked.  <BR>In the process of stalking one he came across another, killed the intended and after a while killed the other that he came across from his research of the other victim. <BR>This may have happened more than once and the other possible victims that he came across while stalking a random victim he never ended up killing due to lack of opportunity or too risky. There may be other victims not linked yet to him that he did kill that may have something in common with his known victims. <BR>So in other words I don&#39;t think you can link all 8 known victims but it may be possible to link two or more of five crime sites and the one aborted crime site. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
