<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7797"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Skov<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Skov<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 17, 2005 - 4:21 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I post this on this thred because it indicates that BTK also took a watch from Nancy Fox, so here is another thing that might be a link between the victims, taking their watches? <BR> <BR>Here is my post from another thred I started on the issue: <BR> <BR> This could indicate that BTK took Nancy Fox´s watch. Never heard this before, anyone?  <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.ksn.com/news/stories/6821422.html" target=_top>http://www.ksn.com/news/stories/6821422.html</a>  <BR> <BR>Nancy Fox´s friend: &#34;I’ve been asked about a watch, too. It hasn’t shown up but I suppose if it does I’ll be asked to ID that too,&#34; she said.  <BR> <BR>So the items that pops up as possible links one way or the other is <BR> <BR>eyeglasses  <BR>watches <BR>jewlery <BR>driverlicences <BR> <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.catchbtk.com/discus/messages/3/498.html?1108570187" target=_top>http://www.catchbtk.com/discus/messages/3/498.html ?1108570187</a><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7797-->
<!--Post: 7848--><!--Time: 1108710169-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7848"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Isleuth<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Isleuth<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 17, 2005 - 11:02 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Skov, <BR>I am really interested in your glasses fetish idea.  I responded to another thread &#40;about the Julie Ladd killing&#41; on the AMW site and linked to your glasses thread on my post because it seems that through the entire messy murder the glasses stayed on.   <BR><a href="http://forums.prospero.com/n/mb/message.asp?webtag=foxamw&amp;msg=1519.1" target=_top>http://forums.prospero.com/n/mb/message.asp?webtag =foxamw&amp;msg=1519.1</a> <BR> <BR>Anyway, the Wichita Eagle article about Shirly Vian&#39;s neighbor Cheryl &#40;who may have been BTKs intended victim that day&#41; states that WPD interviewd her and asked if she wore glasses and if she went to a bar called &#34;A Blackout&#34; here&#39;s the link:  <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.kansas.com/mld/kansas/news/special_packages/btk/10813523.htm" target=_top>http://www.kansas.com/mld/kansas/news/special_pack ages/btk/10813523.htm</a> <BR> <BR>Here is a link to an &#39;A Blackout&#39; website &#40;discussed elsewhere on this site&#41;  <BR> <BR>scroll down to the picture of the pinball machine photograph by a &#34;Tom Bevan&#34;  <BR><a href="http://www.ku.edu/heritage/beats/ablackout.html" target=_top>http://www.ku.edu/heritage/beats/ablackout.html</a>   <BR>Who is the unidentified patron in that photo?  She slightly resembles Nancy Fox to me and  <BR>she&#39;s wearing similar glasses and I&#39;m particulary drawn to the necklace she&#39;s wearing since it is so much  <BR>like the one that WPD think was taken from Fox.  Anyway its kinda  <BR>interesting since the police asked Cheryl if she hung out there as if they  <BR>thought BTK and/or other victims did.   <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7848-->
<!--Post: 7853--><!--Time: 1108711332-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7853"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 17, 2005 - 11:22 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Isleuth, I&#39;ve isolated the picture with this link for easier reference. You can click the picture&#39;s lower right corner to enlarge. <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.ku.edu/heritage/beats/ablackoutpinball.jpg" target=_top>http://www.ku.edu/heritage/beats/ablackoutpinball. jpg</a><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7853-->
<!--Post: 7855--><!--Time: 1108712205-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7855"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Stormy74<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Stormy74<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 17, 2005 - 11:36 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I wonder if any of you are really good with photo enhancing?? Maybe, get in much closer on that necklace. Would be interesting to see what it is up close. I can&#39;t see as well as I used to, but seems it might be some kind of crucifix. Thanks for all the links!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
