<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7859"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 18, 2005 - 12:27 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The victims all have one thing in common, BTK. And since, in his letters, he mentioned that he stalked them, it seems reasonable to assume that he didn&#39;t go door to door looking for victims.  <BR> <BR>What is making it hard to find a common denominator may be looking from the victims point of view. <BR> <BR>Instead of thinking &#34;what were they doing when BTK noticed them&#34;, try thinking &#34;I&#39;m BTK, where do I look for women to stalk?&#34;  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7859-->
<!--Post: 7863--><!--Time: 1108716379-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7863"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Suspiria_2<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Suspiria_2<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 18, 2005 - 12:46 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->it&#39;s extremely difficult to do it from that end, because one can find women to stalk anywhere that women are allowed.   <BR> <BR>that pretty much means anywhere in wichita or elsewhere, excluding most men&#39;s locker rooms or public dressing or bathrooms. <BR> <BR>although i believe i get your drift if you were trying to say that he didn&#39;t round them all up in the same place.  that would be rather like pointing a big finger at himself, and much too simplistic. <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
